150	586,538,806,972	150. Plan of the Cyme.	Plan of a cyme, first stage: a leafy stem ending in a single terminal flower.
151	860,504,1151,974	151. Plan of the Cyme.	The same stem with the terminal flower, a, and a branch from the axil of each uppermost leaf, each ending in a flower-bud, b.
152	1237,505,1610,976	152. Plan of the Cyme.	The side branches branched again in the same way: the middle flower, a, then the flowers b, then the buds c at the outside.
